<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nagarkurnool district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nagarkurnool is a district of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, formed in 2016 from part of Mahbubnagar district. It lies along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> river and includes much of the Nallamala forest and the Amrabad Tiger Reserve. In earlier centuries it held small zamindari estates, such as Jatprole, under the Qutb Shahi sultans and the Nizams.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nagarkurnool-district.jpg" alt="Nagarkurnool district" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: P. Madhusudan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madhava_Swamy_Temple,_Kollapur_Telangana_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
